  "body": "### Summary\nAs the maintainer, I want tests that wait on a fixed sleep to wait on a signal, so that they cannot pass without running the interleaving they document (LESSONS 2) and do not join the flaky list (#704, #772, #521 were the same pattern).\n\n### Scenario\nOn a loaded CI runner, the `handle` task of the blocklist test has not queued its edit when the gate opens; the final lists are the same in both orders, so the test passes without the \"edit queued behind start's read\" case. In `ComposerPlacementTests`, a layout pass slower than the sleep makes a \"nothing changed\" assertion pass before the value could change.\n\n### Evidence (`7a61018f`)\n- `App/SwiftHFRTests/MPStorage/BlocklistSyncTests.swift:251-254`: `let handling = Task { await sync.handle(…) }`, `try await Task.sleep(for: .milliseconds(50))`, `await gate.release()`.\n- `App/SwiftHFRTests/Composer/ComposerPlacementTests.swift:96-100` (and `:122`, `:153`, `:304-368`): `Task.sleep(200 ms)` then a negative assertion.\n- `App/SwiftHFRTests/Composer/ArchivedDraftsTests.swift:198`: same shape.\n\n### Fix\nReplace each sleep with a deterministic signal (a second gate or a counter the fake remote exposes when the edit is queued; a layout probe callback for the hosted tests). A negative is asserted after a positive event that proves the pass ran.\n\n### Proof\nMutation: remove the serialization the BlocklistSync test protects, or the inset rule in `ReaderComposerPresenter.docked`; the rewritten tests fail on every run (not checked today: no mutation was run in this review).\n\nRework model: Sonnet 5.5, reviewed by Opus 5.5.\n\nFound by #775 (cloud/r775-fable, Fable 5.2). Reviewed at `dev-swift` @ `7a61018f`; read from the code, not run on a device unless stated.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
