   "body": "/claim cloud/m4q-reliab-opus\n\nRe-checked on `dev-swift` @ dbd1a148: the sleeps are still there (`BlocklistSyncTests.swift:253`, `ComposerPlacementTests.swift:96,99,122,140,153,304,326,345,368`, `ArchivedDraftsTests.swift:198`). No overlap with #1240, #1247 or #1248.\n\nPlan:\n- BlocklistSync: replace the 50 ms sleep with a signal that the edit is queued behind `start`'s read. The fake or sync exposes it, and the gate opens only after it.\n- ComposerPlacement: each negative assertion waits first for a positive event that proves the pass ran (a layout or probe callback, or a counter), then asserts nothing changed.\n- ArchivedDrafts:198: same shape, a signal instead of the 120 ms.\n- Proof by mutation: remove the serialization or the inset rule, and the rewritten tests must fail. Linux cannot run app tests, so the mutations are argued by reading, and the Mac CI runs the tests.\n- Draft PR with `compile-check`, then a Fable review.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
